{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789922855,"nonce":"8Gx3NqQSV+RsmI9cx9ghJ4j9+i4=","title":"A cast of an f64 to f64 reads the value's bits as an integer","message":"The frontend's array hooks emitted TypedCast { expr: f64-typed call, target_type: f64 } for the storage kind Float (a widening cast that is a no-op for that kind); the boxed read of an array('d') element then printed 6e-323 for 12.0, the bit pattern of the integer 12 as a double. The same cast for i8/i16/i32/u8 to i64 is right. The hook now skips the cast when storage and wide kind agree (cbf3b4a2), so the reproduction needs a hand-built typed AST: a Cast node whose expr is a Call typed f64 and whose target is f64. Find where the typed-AST-to-HIR lowering (or the interpreter) turns a same-type float cast into an int-to-float or bitcast, and make a same-type cast the identity.","files":null}]}